# gate-rules: paths and prerequisites per command. Data only, no logic: the guard scripts read it
# (guard-common.sh gc_rule) and implement each named prerequisite. Design: D2 (onboard redo,
# kit-eval/reviews/jiraiya-onboard-redo-design-20261102.md, "The split").
#
# Format: one rule per line, `<command> <key> <value>`; the value is the rest of the line.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. A key appears once per command.
# Paths are relative to the repository root. Only the onboard entry is filled for now (D2, D3, D4).

# --- onboard (/v0-onboard, guard-onboard.sh) -----------------------------------------------------
onboard phase onboard
onboard feature onboarding
onboard state docs/agents-v0/onboarding/state.json
onboard artifact docs/agents-v0/onboarding/report.md
onboard template docs/agents-v0/onboarding/_report.template.md
# start: prerequisites (checked in this order), then the status it sets.
onboard start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed not-approved not-awaiting-approval
onboard start.status in_progress
onboard start.next Run discovery and write the onboarding docs (report.md and modules/).
# block: the status it sets, and the next step it records when the caller gives none.
onboard block.status blocked
onboard block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-onboard again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready (Design: D3): main session only, after discovery. Runs the baseline audit with --record (a red baseline
# is recorded, not refused), runs the onboarding docs check, then sets the status and the next step below.
onboard ready.requires in-progress
onboard ready.baseline docs/agents-v0/discovery/baseline-audit.txt
onboard ready.status awaiting_approval
onboard ready.next Sensei reviews the onboarding docs and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve onboard
# commit (Design: D4): main session only, after Sensei's approve. Needs onboard approved in the state AND his approval
# record (gc_approval_ok). Stages these paths (those that exist or are tracked; *.lock never), refuses when the index
# already holds another path, secret-scans the staged content, commits once and tags <commit.tag><n>. The pack paths
# are the folders activate-stack-pack.sh writes (.cursor/rules/org, .cursor/skills).
onboard commit.paths docs/agents-v0 README.md .cursor/rules/org .cursor/skills
onboard commit.message onboarding: onboard approved
onboard commit.tag onboard-v
# shown when onboard is already approved (start refuses) and after commit
onboard approved.next /v0-roadmap, /v0-intake, /v0-triage, or /v0-maintain

# --- roadmap (/v0-roadmap, guard-roadmap.sh) -----------------------------------------------------
roadmap phase roadmap
roadmap feature program
roadmap state docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
roadmap artifact docs/agents-v0/roadmap
roadmap template docs/agents-v0/roadmap/_template.md
# check & start: prerequisites
roadmap check.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield not-approved
roadmap validate.sections Problem,Success metric,Options,Chosen option,In scope,Out of scope
roadmap start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield not-awaiting-approval
roadmap start.status in_progress
roadmap start.next Launch the roadmap-planner subagent to draft the roadmap (docs/agents-v0/roadmap/<program>.md).
# block: status and next step
roadmap block.status blocked
roadmap block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-roadmap <discovery-path> again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready: verifies roadmap completeness and sets awaiting_approval
roadmap ready.requires in-progress
roadmap ready.status awaiting_approval
roadmap ready.next Sensei reviews the roadmap and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve roadmap
# commit: checks approval record, stages roadmap files and state, secret-scans, commits and tags
roadmap commit.paths docs/agents-v0/roadmap docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
roadmap commit.message program: roadmap approved
roadmap commit.tag roadmap-v
roadmap approved.next /v0-architecture

# --- architecture (/v0-architecture, guard-architecture.sh) ---------------------------------------
architecture phase architecture
architecture feature program
architecture state docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
architecture artifact docs/agents-v0/architecture.md
# check & start: prerequisites
architecture check.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield roadmap-approved not-approved
architecture start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield roadmap-approved not-awaiting-approval
architecture start.status in_progress
architecture start.next Launch the solution-architect subagent (skill: program-architecture) to author the architecture pack, then launch design-reviewer to write docs/agents-v0/design/system/architecture-review.md.
# block: status and next step
architecture block.status blocked
architecture block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-architecture again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready: verifies architecture pack completeness and zero Open findings in architecture-review.md
architecture ready.requires in-progress
architecture ready.status awaiting_approval
architecture ready.next Sensei reviews the architecture pack and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve architecture
# commit: checks approval record, promotes ADR to Accepted, appends Approved row, runs activate-stack-pack.sh, stages paths, secret-scans, commits and tags
architecture commit.paths docs/agents-v0/architecture.md docs/agents-v0/architecture.phase-result.md docs/agents-v0/network.md docs/agents-v0/adr docs/agents-v0/design/system docs/agents-v0/diagrams docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md docs/agents-v0/program.state.json .cursor/rules/org .cursor/skills .cursor/agents .agents/rules/org .agents/skills .agents/agents
architecture commit.message program: architecture approved
architecture commit.tag architecture-v
architecture approved.next /v0-plan

# --- plan (/v0-plan, guard-plan.sh) -------------------------------------------------------------
plan phase plan
plan feature program
plan state docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
plan artifact docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md
# check & start: prerequisites
plan check.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield architecture-approved not-approved
plan start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed onboard-if-brownfield architecture-approved not-awaiting-approval
plan start.status in_progress
plan start.next Launch the program-planner subagent (skill: program-planning) to author milestone manifests under docs/agents-v0/milestones/ and docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md.
# block: status and next step
plan block.status blocked
plan block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-plan again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready: verifies plan table, flowchart, and story manifests (sentence, surface, size 1-8, no cycles)
plan ready.requires in-progress
plan ready.status awaiting_approval
plan ready.next Sensei reviews the plan manifests and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve plan
# commit: checks approval record, appends Approved row to manifests, stages paths, secret-scans, commits and tags
plan commit.paths docs/agents-v0/milestones docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
plan commit.message program: plan approved
plan commit.tag plan-v
plan approved.next /v0-scaffold

# --- scaffold (/v0-scaffold, guard-scaffold.sh) -------------------------------------------------
scaffold phase scaffold
scaffold feature program
scaffold state docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
scaffold artifact docs/agents-v0/milestones/p0-platform-skeleton.md
# check & start: prerequisites
scaffold check.requires git-work-tree kit-installed greenfield-only plan-approved integration-branch not-approved
scaffold start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed greenfield-only plan-approved integration-branch not-awaiting-approval
scaffold start.status in_progress
scaffold start.next Launch the platform-engineer subagent to configure application scaffold, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, and baseline verify.
# block: status and next step
scaffold block.status blocked
scaffold block.next Fix the blocker, then run /v0-scaffold again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready: verifies native pack verify passes, p0 milestone manifest exists, Dockerfile and Compose exist
scaffold ready.requires in-progress
scaffold ready.status awaiting_approval
scaffold ready.next Sensei reviews the platform skeleton and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve scaffold
# commit: checks approval record, updates p0-platform-skeleton.md status to released with Approved row, stages paths, secret-scans, commits and tags
scaffold commit.paths app Dockerfile docker-compose.yml compose.yaml .dockerignore pom.xml build.gradle package.json pyproject.toml requirements.txt Cargo.toml go.mod docs/agents-v0/milestones docs/agents-v0/program.state.json
scaffold commit.message scaffold: platform skeleton approved
scaffold commit.tag scaffold-v
scaffold approved.next /v0-intake

# --- intake (/v0-intake, guard-intake.sh) -------------------------------------------------------
intake phase intake
intake feature <feature>
intake state docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.state.json
intake artifact docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md
intake result docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.phase-result.md
# check & start: prerequisites
intake check.requires git-work-tree kit-installed integration-branch onboard-if-brownfield plan-if-program scaffold-if-greenfield not-released not-approved
intake start.requires git-work-tree kit-installed integration-branch onboard-if-brownfield plan-if-program scaffold-if-greenfield not-released not-awaiting-approval
intake start.status in_progress
intake start.next Launch the requirements-analyst subagent (skill: spec-intake) to author docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md.
# block: status and next step
intake block.status blocked
intake block.next Resolve the blocker or helper brief, then run /v0-intake <feature> again; it resumes from the files on disk.
# ready: verifies user story, Gherkin AC-1..AC-8, negative/edge + security-trigger refusal, single surface / vertical slice, mandatory sections, and Open questions: none
intake ready.requires in-progress
intake ready.status awaiting_approval
intake ready.next Sensei reviews docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md and runs, in his own terminal outside Cursor: sh .agents-v0/scripts/guard-common.sh approve intake <feature>
# commit: verifies approval record, appends Approved row, runs feature-worktree.sh <feature>, stages intake files in the worktree, secret-scans, and commits "<story>: intake approved" on feature/<feature>
intake commit.paths docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.state.json docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.phase-result.md
intake commit.message <story>: intake approved
intake approved.next /v0-design <feature>
